## 11. YAML Schema Specification (Draft)

### Agent Definition
```yaml
agents:
  - name: <agent-name>
    description: <human-readable description>
    llm:
      provider: "lmstudio" | "ollama" | "llamacpp"
      base_url: <http-url>  # For lmstudio
      model_path: <path>     # For llamacpp
      model: <model-name>
      backend: "vulkan" | "cuda" | "metal"
      n_gpu_layers: <int>
    tools:
      - file-read
      - file-write
      - file-search
      - file-move
      - file-delete
      - grep
      - web-fetch
      - web-scrape
      - web-search
      - shell-exec
      - shell-safe
      - memory-save
      - memory-load
      - log-write
```

### Workflow Definition
```yaml
workflow:
  - step: <human-readable step name>
    agent: <agent-name>
    parallel: true | false
    input:
      <step-specific-input>
    output:
      <step-specific-output>
```

### Example: Full Workflow
```yaml
agents:
  - name: file-analyzer
    description: Analyzes code and finds patterns
    llm:
      provider: "lmstudio"
      base_url: "http://localhost:1234/v1"
      model: "openai/gpt-oss-20b"
      backend: "vulkan"
    tools:
      - file-read
      - file-search
      - grep

  - name: web-scraper
    description: Scrapes web content for research
    llm:
      provider: "lmstudio"
      base_url: "http://localhost:1234/v1"
      model: "openai/gpt-oss-20b"
    tools:
      - web-fetch
      - web-scrape

workflow:
  - step: Analyze codebase
    agent: file-analyzer
    input:
      path: "./src/"
      pattern: "async function"

  - step: Research documentation
    agent: web-scraper
    input:
      urls:
        - https://docs.rs/tokio
        - https://docs.rs/serde

  - step: Generate report
    agent: file-analyzer
    input:
      template: report.md.j2
      output: ./analysis-report.md
```

